From 8b510fb61cccb2440ed669c21c7c197d7d4f0c72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bren Marshall <brenallenmarshall@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:17:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(ui): add --no-activate and --minimized start options

A launched window always took the foreground: winit shows a visible,
active window with SW_SHOW, and the shell also called focus_window().
--no-activate creates the window inactive and skips focus_window().
--minimized also minimizes it at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
